                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "There is already a patch up that actually enables the LogService support for multi-host [1].\n\n[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/85600"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "That patch is up since November of last year. I already reviewed it, but good to link it here also for context.\n\nHowever it's 5 patches into a relation  chain so it's unclear when it will merge.\n\nThis patch solves the immediate problem of bmcweb **failing** the redfish validator. It's quick fix until something better like 85600 gets reviewed.\n\nOverall i don't think a 'better' solution existing is able to block simpler fixes. \n\nIf that were the case we could never merge anything because somewhere someone is always working on a better / more complete solution."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Let's add a comment as to why here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "You might use the `BMCWEB_REDFISH_EVENTLOG_LOCATION == \"managers\"` instead?  Or in addition."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Changed it here to make a more informed choice as to which link to append and under which circumstances.\n\nI'm assuming both event log backends currently do not support per-host entries so  i only put the per-system log link in the non multi-host case.\n\nThanks for the feedback and please review again \ud83d\udc4d"
                }
            ],
