        {
            "number": 5,
            "revision": "c120f06ff0d122a79bf9bd3ba3b3a6c2c72e4beb",
            "parents": [
                "2bd69f6557d59391a236f9bdf61b7a6d4b77f295"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/82/87082/5",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "createdOn": 1775745843,
            "author": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Did redfish service validator get run, per TESTING.md?  I suspect it would've caught the bug below."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "The reason i post patches like this is to make the validator fully pass for single and multi-host build configuration on all systems i have access to for development.\n\nBecause i am too lazy to run it partially or pick out specific trees to run it on - and due to the links it will visit most of the tree anyways...\n\nI run it as documented in `TESTING.md`\n\n`/tmp/rsv-venv/bin/rf_service_validator --auth Session \\\n-i https://s5549-bmc-a0423f63b4a5.lab.9e.network:443 -u root -p *******`\n\n> I suspect it would've caught the bug below.\n\nno - it does not catch link bugs like this, at least not the one i have."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 218,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "ACK."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please do research into how redfish odata trees work.  If you need help, I'm always available on discord to help you 1:1, but as written this patch is broken assuming you can arbitrarily change URIs in an Odata model. The URIs are specified by the tree itself.\n\nI suspect redfish service validator would've flagged this, but if you ran it and it didnt', I can open a bug with DMTF.  Please let me know if you're seeing a passing result with this, if so it's a test bug."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Right, i looked again in section `9.6.13 Links`\n\nand it makes a clear distinction between `subordinate reference property` and `associated reference property` and where they go in a response.\n\nI will try to keep this in mind for future patches \ud83d\udc4d\n\n> If you need help, I'm always available on discord to help you 1:1,\n\nappreciate it \ud83d\udcaf\n\n\n>  Please let me know if you're seeing a passing result with this, if so it's a test bug.\n\nYes, if we put\n```\n\"LogServices\": {\n    \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices\"\n},\n```\nthen RSV gets an almost clean run `Summary - PASS: 6613, WARN: 357, FAIL: 2, NOT TESTED: 7504` (the 2 fails are unrelated)\n\nI ran with up-to-date RSV and following command\n\n```\n/tmp/rsv-venv/bin/rf_service_validator --auth Session \\\n-i https://s5549-bmc-a0423f63b4a5.lab.9e.network:443 -u root -p *******\n```\n\nthe 'LogServices' property is marked PASS on `/redfish/v1/Systems/Tyan_S5549_Baseboard` response.\n```\nLogServices\n[Link to: /redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices]\n        PASS\n```\n\nAgree it's a good idea to let the validator check for bugs like this, would be nice if you can poke them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> would be nice if you can poke them.\n\nhttps://redfishforum.com/ if you don't have a CLA, or if you're in their causeway, you can just get on the Redfish-tools meeting to ask about it.  If i get a free second, I can too.\n\nThis comment needs to remain open, because regardless of whether or not the tools catch it, it's not clear to me it's correct.  I could always be wrong though, but would need the standards body help to know that this URI is actually correct."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "FYI: as part of adding multi-host PostCode LogService I have already enabled the collection in this patch: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/85600/11 .."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I opened an issue here\n\nhttps://github.com/DMTF/Redfish-Service-Validator/issues/663\n\nsince i agree with your spec interpretation.\n\nIf the maintainers there are unsure, i can take it back to Redfish forum.\n\n\nSeparately of the tooling issue, does the current patchset work for you?\n\nWith the current revision it's just extra guards around an optional property, which should be fine, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Just to sync with the RSV issue \"Technically per the schema definition this is valid, but I agree in this case this does not seem like a correct usage of the property\"\n\nThat's roughly my understanding as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Separately of the tooling issue, does the current patchset work for you?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Calling this only a tooling issue is incorrect.  This is a functional issue with the patch that the tooling happens to not catch."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah but that was patchset 5 right?\n\nI have made changes since then which should sidestep this issue entirely.\nAt least i believe so.\n\nAre you saying patchset 7 still has a Redfish spec violation?\n\nHow can i move forward here or which changes would you like to see in this patch to fix the validation error on multi-host Redfish.\n\n> This is a functional issue with the patch that the tooling happens to not catch.\n\nWith functional issue you mean that the link is only provided for some combination of meson options (inconsistency) ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3084,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "You appear to have misunderstood how Redfish trees work.  You cannot just redirect arbitrary NavigationLinks of the tree to different trees, even if they are the same type."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3084,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yep - thanks for the clarification \ud83d\udc4d"
                }
            ],
